          "note": "Topic 14.4.3, printed page 308."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Sulfur has two oxides, sulfur dioxide and sulfur trioxide, collectively SOx. They are emitted primarily by burning coal and oil. When SOx combines with water vapour it causes acid rain, which damages ecosystems; SO2 is the major source of acid deposition in the air."
          }
        ]
      }
    }
